2026-06-01 16:26:40,172 | AGENT | Legal Agent answered: Based on our company context, we note that the solution must be designed as a tool of assistance, with no decision automated without explicit validation of an agent, which aligns with our policy of no automated decision without human validation. We also have expertise in EU AI Act, prohibited AI practices awareness, limited risk AI transparency obligations, and human oversight contractual enforcement, which should help us meet the explainability and transparency requirements.

As for regulatory compliance, we are aware of the need to respect the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) and have a standard legal basis for data processing under Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest. We also have a data protection agreement template version 3.2 and can provide support for data protection impact assessments.

