2026-06-01 16:31:38,179 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is pleased to submit a comprehensive tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily tasks, aligning with the City of Belval's digital transformation strategy. Our proposed solution leverages expertise in large language models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation capabilities, ensuring compliance with EU data protection regulations.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an intelligent assistance tool that integrates with existing practices, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and complies with regulatory constraints. The solution must provide quick access to reliable information, facilitate drafting administrative contents, assist in file analysis, and ensure collaboration and continuity among agents.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution will utilize the Mistral 7B Instruct model, which offers strong performance in French-language tasks and is self-hostable, ensuring compliance with EU data protection regulations. The AI components will include a combination of natural language processing and information retrieval techniques to facilitate access to internal procedures, regulatory texts, and relevant documents.

The solution will be designed as a tool of assistance, with no decision automated without explicit validation of an agent, aligning with our policy of no automated decision without human validation. We will implement explainability and transparency features, including source citation and chain-of-thought display capabilities, enabling agents to understand the reasoning behind provided answers and suggestions.

To ensure security and compliance, we will enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and implement role-based access control (RBAC). Our network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns. We will also conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA) with an average duration of 3 weeks.

The hosting will be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, with a particular attention to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. Our green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, use 100% renewable energy and have low Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) values of 1.3 and 1.28 respectively.

Our budget for the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that will remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. We target a gross margin percentage of 28% and have a minimum acceptable margin percentage of 18%.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
The call for tenders requires the solution to provide times of response compatible with daily use by agents, with an indicative time of response lower than 2 seconds. While our technical architecture has achieved a p95 response time of 1800 ms for RAG solutions, which is below the expected time of response, further evaluation would be necessary to confirm whether our solution can meet this requirement.

# 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is confident that our proposed solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for an intelligent assistance tool that integrates with existing practices, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and complies with regulatory constraints. We are committed to delivering a high-quality solution that supports the City's digital transformation strategy while minimizing its environmental footprint.

Our team is experienced in managing large projects, with a largest project managed being 4.5 million euros. We have a team of certified project managers, including 5 PMP-certified PMs, and our typical delivery structure includes phases like Inception & Design, Pilot/MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support.

We believe that our proposed solution offers the best value for the City of Belval and look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail.
